  "description": "Change of use from Use Class C3 (dwelling house) to Use Class Sui Generis (HMO-house in multiple occupation) for 8 persons, including single storey rear to side extension, conversion of garage to habitable room with changes to front facade, extension of roof at side to form gable, rear dormer, front roof lights and provision of refuse and cycle storage.",
  "development_type": "Other change of use",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Notwithstanding the approved plans, prior to first occupation of the development hereby permitted, details of the design and siting of refuse storage facilities including facilities for the recycling of waste to satisfy the future number of occupiers on site, shall be submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority, in accordance with the Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (2024). Once approved the development shall be carried out in accordance with the approved details prior to first occupation and retained for the lifetime of the development.\r \rReason: In order to facilitate efficient, safe and clean removal of household refuse, the location and accessibility of refuse storage plus to maintain safety on the Highway.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied until the 9 long stay cycle parking spaces have been fully constructed in accordance with the hereby approved details and shall thereafter be retained for the lifetime of the development.  \r \rReason: To ensure that adequate cycle parking facilities are provided to promote sustainable modes of transport. \r",
    "Notwithstanding submitted approved plans, the rear loft space windows serving bedrooms 7 and 8 shall not be obscure glazed to provides adequate levels of daylight to the bedrooms.\r\rReason: To ensure an acceptable standard of accommodation for future occupiers, in accordance with Policy DMD8 of the Enfield Development Management Document and Policy D6 of the London Plan.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall not be occupied by more than eight residents at any one time without first obtaining the approval, in writing, of the Local Planning Authority.  \r \rReason: To ensure that the future occupation of the building does not adversely affect the adjoining premises/immediate \r",
    "No cooking facilities, including hot plates, shall be installed in the bedrooms of the development hereby permitted unless details have first been submitted to and approved in writing by the local planning authority. Any cooking facilities shall thereafter only be implemented in accordance with the details that have been approved pursuant to this condition. \r \rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area. \r",
    "The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\r\rE00, E01, E02, E03, E04, E05, P01, P02, P03, P04, P05 and P06, SuDS proforma, Highway Safety Impact Assessment, Parking Survey & CIL form\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning."
  ],
